Chapter: BvtHouseOf
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositeGameRules
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 cgg-house-of names cgg-lodges once a call (a list constant is built again at every mention): the boot's bed census
 kept 168 MB when each step named it. Answers a bit per check: 1 a home on the first house's floor is house 0, 2 a home
 in no house is -1, 4 a call that walks every lodge allocates under 8 KB (it was 88 KB). 7 is all.
  bho-run : Integer -> Integer
  bho-run (unused) = let first = (list-at cgg-houses 0).floor
    in let inside = BbSpot { x = first.x1, y = first.y1, z = 0 }
    in let nowhere = BbSpot { x = 1, y = 1, z = 0 }
    in let found = if cgg-house-of inside 0 == 0 then 1 else 0
    in let t0 = __heap-save
    in let missed = cgg-house-of nowhere 0
    in let t1 = __heap-save
    in let none = if missed == -1 then 2 else 0
    in let cheap = if t1 - t0 < 8192 then 4 else 0
    in found + none + cheap
  bvt-house-of : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-house-of (unused) = act
    n <- bho-run 0
    a <- bvt-check ("cgg-house-of finds a home's house and walks the lodges without rebuilding them at each step (code " & show n & ")") (n == 7)
    a
  end
